program	errors/ref_static_declaration.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	same
expect	error
build	refused	static `SLOT` may not be a reference: `&Int` is a reference, and references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not escape it (designs 88/106)
meets_expect	yes
log	"error: static `SLOT` may not be a reference: `&Int` is a reference, and references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not escape it (designs 88/106)"
log	"  --> examples/errors/ref_static_declaration.saw:14:1"
log	"     |"
log	" 14 | static SLOT: &Int = 0"
log	"     | ^"
log	"   hint: use the value type (`Int`), or — to hand out storage a type already owns — declare a `borrows` accessor (`... borrows -> &var Int` with `lend`, design 141)"
log	""
log	"error: static `SLOT` has type `&Int` but its initializer has type `Int`"
log	"  --> examples/errors/ref_static_declaration.saw:14:1"
log	"     |"
log	" 14 | static SLOT: &Int = 0"
log	"     | ^"
log	""
log	"error: static `SLOT` has non-Sync type `&Int`; statics must be Sync (shared across all tasks)"
log	"  --> examples/errors/ref_static_declaration.saw:14:1"
log	"     |"
log	" 14 | static SLOT: &Int = 0"
log	"     | ^"
log	"   hint: use a Sync type — mutation of global state flows only through interior-synchronized types like `Atomic<Int>` and `SpinLock<T>`, or declare an `unsafe static var` and own the serialization argument."
